go-picomatch
============

A Go port of picomatch, produced for Port Mortem 2026 (Track F, JavaScript -> Go).

This product includes software developed by Jon Schlinkert and the micromatch
contributors.


Upstream work
-------------

  picomatch v4.0.5
  https://github.com/micromatch/picomatch
  commit 4f41a8edade7a5ab19832f7b40ecce46b288767f
  Copyright (c) 2017-present, Jon Schlinkert
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The upstream project is vendored under `tests/original/`, byte-for-byte
unmodified, together with its own test suite. Its licence is preserved at
`tests/original/LICENSE`, and every vendored file is hashed in
`tests/original/MANIFEST.json`.

The vendored JavaScript exists for two build-time purposes only:

  1. Recording picomatch's observable behaviour while its own unmodified test
     suite runs, which produces the fixtures in `testdata/original/`.
  2. Differential testing of the Go port against the original.

It is never executed by, linked into, or shelled out to by the Go package. The
Go package imports nothing outside the standard library.


